```cedar
// Close a work order only at MAIN, and only with a granted approval for that
// same work order that came from someone other than the agent.
permit (
  principal,
  action == AOB::Action::"close_workorder",
  resource
)
when {
  context.input.site_id == "MAIN" &&
  context has approval &&
  context.approval.status == PGI::ApprovalStatus::"APPR" &&
  context.approval.wonum == context.input.wonum &&
  context.approval.site_id == context.input.site_id &&
  context.approval.approver != principal
};

// List work orders only when the request explicitly names MAIN.
permit (
  principal,
  action == AOB::Action::"list_workorders",
  resource
)
when {
  context.input has site_id &&
  context.input.site_id has typeChoice0 &&
  context.input.site_id.typeChoice0 == "MAIN"
};
```

I wrote this policy for closing work orders at MAIN, as you asked. The `close_workorder` tool description says "Do not use for work orders at site MAIN", which contradicts your intent. The policy follows your intent, but the tool itself may reject those calls.

I treated "granted" as approval status `APPR` only. A status such as `WAPPR` (still waiting) does not count.
